<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Haydaran</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1052</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Haydaran was fought in April 1052 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> between the army of the Zirid emir al-Mu'izz ibn Badis and the Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hilal">Banu Hilal</a> tribes, sent west after the Zirids broke with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>. Despite their greater numbers the Zirids were routed. The defeat left the countryside open to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> was abandoned in 1057, and the Zirids withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a>.</p></div>
